  ('1c00114c-8d67-5498-8e77-a16a6bc51897', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The ranger told us about the moose that was spotted near the campground at breakfast." The ranger spoke to the group during breakfast. Which revision places the prepositional phrase so the sentence says this clearly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"At breakfast, the ranger told us about the moose that was spotted near the campground.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The ranger told us about the moose that was spotted at breakfast near the campground.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-prepositional-phrase"},{"text":"The ranger told us about the moose at breakfast that was spotted near the campground.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-prepositional-phrase"},{"text":"The ranger told us about the moose that was spotted near the campground eating breakfast.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-modifier"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At breakfast, the ranger told us about the moose that was spotted near the campground.$q$, $q$Moving "At breakfast" to the front makes it modify "told," so it is clear when the ranger spoke. The other versions leave the phrase near "moose" or "spotted," which suggests the moose was at breakfast or was spotted then.$q$, 'draft', null)
