   $q$Read the sentence: "Riding the train into the city is often faster than ___." Which choice completes the comparison with parallel structure?$q$, $q$[{"text":"driving there during rush hour","is_correct":true},{"text":"when you drive there during rush hour","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"to drive there during rush hour","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"infinitive-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"if drivers go there during rush hour","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-breaks-parallel"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$driving there during rush hour$q$, $q$The sentence compares "Riding the train," a gerund phrase, with another way of traveling, so the match is the gerund phrase "driving there." "To drive there" uses an infinitive, which does not line up with "Riding."$q$, 'draft', null)
