   $q$Read the sentence: "By next June, the bridge crew will have repainted every railing." Which words make up the verb phrase in this sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"the bridge crew","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-noun-verb"},{"text":"By next June","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-prepositional-verb"},{"text":"will have repainted","is_correct":true},{"text":"every railing","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-noun-verb"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$will have repainted$q$, $q$A verb phrase is the main verb plus its helping verbs, so "will have repainted" is the verb phrase. "By next June" is a prepositional phrase that tells when, and the other choices are noun phrases.$q$, 'draft', null)
