   $q$Read the sentence: "The guide gave three rules for the greenhouse tour: stay on the paths, keep your hands off the orchids, and ___." Which choice completes the list with parallel structure?$q$, $q$[{"text":"quiet voices","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"noun-phrase-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"speak quietly","is_correct":true},{"text":"speaking quietly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gerund-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"you should speak quietly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-breaks-parallel"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$speak quietly$q$, $q$The first two rules are commands that begin with a base verb ("stay," "keep"), so the third should too: "speak quietly." "Speaking quietly" changes to a gerund and breaks the pattern.$q$, 'draft', null)
