  ('f6906750-a70e-54bc-a60e-5f3861bb7d02', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentences: "Amara studied the star chart. She noticed a pattern in the planets' positions. She reported it to her astronomy club." Which revision uses a participial phrase to combine them correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Studying the star chart, a pattern in the planets' positions caught Amara's eye, and she reported it to her astronomy club.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier"},{"text":"Studying the star chart, Amara noticed a pattern in the planets' positions and reported it to her astronomy club.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Amara studied the star chart, noticed a pattern in the planets' positions, and her astronomy club received a report of it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"Amara, who studied the star chart, noticed a pattern in the planets' positions, she reported it to her astronomy club.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Studying the star chart, Amara noticed a pattern in the planets' positions and reported it to her astronomy club.$q$, $q$"Studying the star chart" correctly modifies Amara, the subject, and the compound verb "noticed ... and reported" keeps the actions parallel. In the first choice, the participial phrase modifies "a pattern," which could not study a chart, so the modifier dangles.$q$, 'draft', null)
