   $q$Which sentence uses parallel structure correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The internship taught Lucia how to build a website, testing it, and to explain its features to clients.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-forms-in-series"},{"text":"The internship taught Lucia how to build a website, how to test it, and how to explain its features to clients.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The internship taught Lucia to build a website, test it, and how to explain its features to clients.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-forms-in-series"},{"text":"The internship taught Lucia building a website, to test it, and explaining its features to clients.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-forms-in-series"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The internship taught Lucia how to build a website, how to test it, and how to explain its features to clients.$q$, $q$Each item in the correct sentence follows the same "how to" plus verb pattern. The third choice starts with plain infinitives but switches to "how to" for the last item, so the series is not parallel.$q$, 'draft', null)
